window.docContents[156].resolve({"/ISO-80000-8-___-Acoustics/The-algebraic-Remarks-as-kind-laws___-linear-acoustics-built-by-the-kind-algebra/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--ISO-80000-8-___-Acoustics--The-algebraic-Remarks-as-kind-laws___-linear-acoustics-built-by-the-kind-algebra":{"contents":"Several Part-8 definitions state a quantity's defining relation algebraically — the\nconstitutive laws of linear acoustics. Sound particle velocity is the time-derivative of\ndisplacement (8-4), acceleration of velocity (8-5); sound intensity is the product of\nsound pressure and particle velocity (8-10, I = p·u); the two impedances are quotients\nof sound pressure (8-12, 8-13). Each is specified as an R12 kind-law, the kinematics\ncrossing to ISO 80000-3 for time.\n\n\n\nSound intensity is sound pressure × particle velocity — a verified construction (item\n8-10). A sound intensity built as the product of a sound pressure and a particle velocity\ncarries its product certificate by construction, over the ℝ carrier. The companion\nsoundIntensity_dim_from_pressure_velocity shows the intensity is M·T⁻³ because the\nlength in pressure and velocity cancels — the acoustic intensity law as a checked\ncomputation. Uses the quotient kind-law.\n\nsoundIntensityOf p u := Quantity.mul soundIntensity_prod_pressure_velocity p u, and\nsoundIntensityOf_isProduct is rfl. The same family gives the quotient constructors\ncharacteristicImpedanceOf (= p/u) and the cross-part kinematic laws\nparticleVelocity_quot_displacement_duration (= displacement / time), the time crossing\nto ISO 80000-3.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009ISO 80000-8 — Acoustics","header":"24.4. The algebraic Remarks as kind-laws: linear acoustics built by the kind algebra","id":"/ISO-80000-8-___-Acoustics/The-algebraic-Remarks-as-kind-laws___-linear-acoustics-built-by-the-kind-algebra/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--ISO-80000-8-___-Acoustics--The-algebraic-Remarks-as-kind-laws___-linear-acoustics-built-by-the-kind-algebra"},"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/What-a-vocabulary-answers-for-___-the-coverage-censuses/#annotation-kindDiagnostic":{"contents":"Not an exception but an enrollment, on a KindOfProperty: the kind is a quality or\nconditioning output a consumer must read, and the string says what it diagnoses.\n\n/-- A quality kind the retrieval exports: marked diagnostic, and carried by a produced\nport of `Good.invBoundary` below. -/\n@[kindDiagnostic \"whether the retrieval's answer was decided inside its domain\"]\ndef qcK : KindOfProperty := { id := \"contract coverage probe quality\", scale := .ordinal }\n\n\n#kind_diagnostic_coverage then asks the declared boundaries in scope for a produced port\ncarrying it; a marked kind no boundary exports is a side channel. An unmarked kind is not\nwalked, so removing the mark is the exemption, and a scope with no marks records that\nvisibly. Rejected at elaboration unless the declaration is a KindOfProperty and the\ndescription is non-empty.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009What a vocabulary answers for — the coverage censuses","header":"31.7.4. @[kindDiagnostic \"…\"]  — a conditioning output, enrolled","id":"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/What-a-vocabulary-answers-for-___-the-coverage-censuses/#annotation-kindDiagnostic"}});